  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\int_{0}^{5} \\max \\left\\{x^{2}, 6 x-8\\right\\} d x$\r\nLet $f(x)=x^{2}-6 x+8$\r\n$\\quad=(x-4)(x-2)$\r\n$\\therefore$ For $x \\in[0,2] \\cup[4,5], f(x)>0$ and in $x \\in[2,4], f(x)     < 0$\r\n$\\int_{0}^{5} \\max \\left(x^{2}, 6 x-8\\right)=\\int_{0}^{2} x^{2} d x+\\int_{2}^{4}(6 x-8) d x+\\int_{4}^{5} x^{2} d x=\\frac{8}{3}+20+\\frac{61}{3}=43$"
  }
}